From f5cc9ba9c086fa3582434a85b631fafd71240991 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:12:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: say which audio outputs are in use, and where their
 sound goes, to the windowing system

The windowing system turns off, ten seconds after Kodi comes up, the outputs
that Kodi does not draw on. An HDMI or DisplayPort output carries sound only
while its CRTC is on, so a receiver or a sound bar on such an output lost its
sound device. To keep that output on without any file (the next commit), the
windowing system has to know which audio outputs are in use and which graphics
output carries each one. The kernel has no link from a PCM to a connector; what
there is, and what this records:

- Where the sound card is: the PCI address of its device, the nearest PCI device
  on the way of /sys/class/sound/cardN/device (the card of a SOF machine driver
  is a platform device under the controller), and the devices that the
  controller is a consumer of ("supplier:pci:<address>" links in its sysfs
  folder, Linux drivers/base/core.c devlink_add_symlinks(); the i915 audio
  component adds one from the Intel HD Audio controller to the graphics,
  intel_audio.c device_link_add()). Only sysfs is read: nothing is opened.
  (CAEDeviceInfo::m_cardDevice, m_cardSuppliers.)
- Whether the PCM of an output plays to a graphics output: ALSA gives the PCMs of
  HDMI and DisplayPort outputs an ELD control. GetELD() records whether it found
  one; for a PCM that is not named as an HDMI one it is asked on its own, and the
  ELD read for the identity of its display only, nothing else of the output
  changed (CAEDeviceInfo::m_displayPcm).
- Who the display is: its ELD identity (maker, product, name), which Hades
  already reads (KODI::UTILS::IdentityOfEld()).

The engine publishes, on its own thread, each time it loads its settings or
opens its sink (CActiveAE::PublishSoundOutputs()): the outputs of the two
settings (the passthrough one only with passthrough on), the ones used for them
(FollowDisplay(), and the first output in place of Kodi's "Default", as the
sink opens it), and the one that the sink opened. For each: whether a graphics
output carries it, who its display is, and where its card is. An output whose
ELD has no display now (the windowing system turned its output off, and an
output that is off has no ELD) is given with the last display read of it in
this run. The windowing system reads the list with no lock held but while a
copy is made (KODI::UTILS::CSoundOutputsInUse, a generation that goes up only
when what is said changes).

Nothing else changes in what the engine does or lists. Tested on the host
(the published list); the rest is read and syntax-checked against the build's
own compile commands. What ALSA and sysfs give on each machine, only hardware
shows.
